@page "/styleguide"
@rendermode @(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))

<!-- 
  Styleguide is now DRIVEN BY THE LIVE UNIFIED CSS (css/chatfish.css).
  - No more self-contained <style> duplicating the palette.
  - Swatches use var(--xxx) so they stay in sync with the real design tokens.
  - Added "Live UI Components" section using the actual classes from the app
    (conversation items, messages, buttons, forms, etc.).
  - Single source of truth: edit css/chatfish.css and both the real UI + this guide update.
-->

<h1 style="margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 32px; font-weight: 600;">Chatfish Style Guide</h1>

<p style="color: #666; max-width: 640px;">
  All styles come from the single unified <code>css/chatfish.css</code> (loaded globally by the host shell for server pages and WASM).
  Design tokens live in <code>:root</code> and are used everywhere via <code>var(--name)</code>.
</p>

